{
  "spec": "enginespace/references-cases@1",
  "about": "Good and bad references manifests (enginespace/references@1, ARCHITECTURE section 9.7) and the verdict that both ends have to give: the zod schema in packages/schema/references.ts (tests/schema/references.test.ts) and the grader's check, the JSON Schema and the rules after it (labs/grader/tests/test_fetch.py). A case is a whole `manifest`, or `entries`: each is the `base` entry with the keys of that object set over it, and `$remove` names keys to take out. `where` lists the JSON Pointers of the places the problems are at, when the two ends put them in the same place; `null` is a verdict only (a missing key, which zod reports at the key and JSON Schema at the object). Synthetic: every hash is that of the word example, every host is example.invalid or this machine, and no file exists.",
